{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548615-can-mages-soak-paradox-damage","id":1548615,"title":"Can mages soak Paradox damage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-20T08:07:41-08:00","id":1548615,"title":"Can mages soak Paradox damage?","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> I was wondering if Paradox damage is meant to be soakable, or is considered automatic.<br /> If we look over the chart, 6-10 Backlash successes would still inflict 1 Bashing damage per success, without the alternative to opt into something else. That will most likely mean sending the Mage into incapacitation, with 3 Lethal damage and 5 Bashing (after the Bashing turns into Lethal for being incapacitated). That sounds like a certain death if you're missing a few health levels.<br /> <br /> If we look over 11-15 things get even worse, who on earth would be able to absorb 11 to 15 Lethal without dying on the spot?<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/gUL9gri.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T09:45:47-08:00","id":1548617,"title":"","content":"Honestly i do not do dmg in paradox backlashes, its way more fun to do a geenie and make the punishment fit the crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T13:08:00-08:00","id":1548631,"title":"","content":"It looks like that's the Revised chart in... which was published with massive errors... in the M20 format. The M20 version corrected it, as did one of the Revised authors back in the day. Where ever it says &quot;level&quot; of damage, it should be &quot;die&quot; of damage (I checked, both versions in my copy of M20 since that chart is in two places in that tome, both say &quot;die&quot; not &quot;level&quot; so unless they edited the pdfs and my physical copy and pdfs are out of date, I'm confident that there's an edition issue at hand).<br /> <br /> So if you get 10 successes on your Paradox roll, you take 10 <b>dice</b> of lethal damage, not 10 <b>levels</b>. While that's and massive a dangerous Backlash, odds are you don't die from it regardless of soak.<br /> <br /> That said, Paradox damage is soakable, even if most mages can't soak lethal or agg damage naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}